   "iso_sim": true,
   "status": "original",
   "story": "Cold daylight, deep blacks, one warm accent per frame. An original colour simulation from the Cinema Collection, built from a visual study of HANA-BI (1997, directed by Takeshi Kitano, cinematography by Hideo Yamamoto): bright cool daylight exteriors, the first of Kitano's films to shoot in strong sun, with the blue living in the locations, costumes and light itself rather than tinted onto skin, near-neutral flesh tones, dense blacks kept open with midtones intact and bright areas rolling off soft, and isolated warm accents — bonfire, fireworks, blood — the only heat in the frame. Grain and bloom here are our own choices inferred from a 35mm negative at the period's shooting speeds; neither is documented for the film itself. No single frame, still or poster from the film was copied; every parameter here is our own colour science.",
